== input
sentence #12  10:00.000 → 10:31.340
  text:  So what we want to do today is look at how a block cipher like AES actually works inside, because once you understand the round structure, the key schedule and the way the S-boxes give you confusion, you will see why the attacks we discussed last week do not apply to it, and why people still trust it after more than twenty years of public analysis by some of the best cryptographers in the world.
